      "source_line_start": 206,
      "source_line_end": 231,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{definition}[Epsilon Characterization of the Infimum]\n\\label{def:epsilon-characterization-of-infimum}\nLet $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$ be nonempty and bounded below, and let\n$i\\in\\mathbb{R}$. Then\n\\[\n  i=\\inf A\n\\]\nif and only if both of the following conditions hold:\n\\[\n  (\\forall a\\in A)(i\\leq a),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n  (\\forall\\varepsilon>0)(\\exists a\\in A)(a<i+\\varepsilon).\n\\]\nEquivalently,\n\\[\n  i=\\inf A\n  \\Longleftrightarrow\n  \\left[\n    (\\forall a\\in A)(i\\leq a)\n    \\land\n    (\\forall\\varepsilon>0)(\\exists a\\in A)(i\\leq a<i+\\varepsilon)\n  \\right].\n\\]\n\\end{definition}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
  "creation_mode": "prompt"
